hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7227","The best of my Umma would be those of the generation nearest to mine. Then those nearest to them, then those nearest to them, then people would come whose witness would precede the oath and the oath will precede the witness. Hannad has not made the mention of Qarn in his narration. Qutaiba said that, instead of the word Qaum, the word Aqwam has been used. (Using translation from Muslim 2533a)"
"7228","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The best people are those of my generation, and then those who will come after them (the next generation), and then those who will come after them (i.e. the next generation), and then after them, there will come people whose witness will precede their oaths, and whose oaths will precede their witness."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 6429)"
"7229","The best of my people are those of my generation, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then those who come after them."
"7230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Glad tidings for the person who visited me and believed in me, and glad tidings and even more glad tidings for the one who believed in me even though he did not see me."
"7231","The people most loved by me from amongst my Ummah would be those who would come after me but everyone amongst them would have the keenest desire to catch a glimpse of me even at the cost of his family and wealth. (Using translation from Muslim 2832)"
"7232","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): “Glad tidings to the person who visited me and believed in me, and seven times glad tidings to the person who believed in me even though he did not see me.”"
"7233","The narrator named Ayman heard this narration from both Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him). This narrator named Ayman is Ayman bin Malik Ash'ari."
"7234","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) recited Allah Almighty’s statement about Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) (the command of Allah"
"7235","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the statement of Allah regarding Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him). (Sayyiduna Ibrahim [peace be upon him] said:) ""O my Lord! Indeed, they (the idols) have led many people astray. So whoever follows me, he is of me, and whoever disobeys me, then surely You are Most Forgiving, Most Merciful."" (The statement of Allah is:) Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) said: ""If You punish them, they are Your servants."" (The narrator states:) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised both his hands and supplicated: O Allah, (forgive) my Ummah, (forgive) my Ummah. So Allah Almighty said: O Jibreel! Go to Muhammad (the Prophet [peace and blessings of Allah be upon him] says) Your Lord knows best (but still He said): Ask him why he is weeping. So Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about it. Then Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him) conveyed the Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reply to Allah Almighty, although Allah knows best. Allah Almighty said: O Jibreel! Go to Muhammad and say: We will please you regarding your Ummah. We will not disgrace you."
"7236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes, it was a prayer in which both longing and awe were present. During it, I asked my Lord about three things; He granted me two of them and did not grant me one. I requested Him not to destroy us as He destroyed the previous nations, so He granted me this. I asked Him not to impose upon us an enemy from other nations who would overpower us, so He granted me this as well. I asked Him not to divide us into groups, but He did not grant me this."
"7237","I asked my Lord three things and He has granted me two but has withheld one. I begged my Lord that my Ummah should not be destroyed because of famine and He granted me this. And I begged my Lord that my Ummah should not be destroyed by drowning (by deluge) and He granted me this. And I begged my Lord that there should be no bloodshed among the people of my Ummah, but He did not grant it. (Using translation from Muslim 2890a)"
"7238","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: Allah, the Exalted, folded for me the earth, or he said (the narrator is doubtful): My Lord folded for me the earth, so much so that I saw its easts and wests (i.e. the extremities). The kingdom of my community will reach as far as the earth was floded for me. The two treasures, the red and the white, were bestowed on me. I prayed to my Lord that He may not destroy my community by prevailing famine, and not give their control to an enemy who annihilates then en masse except from among themselves. My Lord said to me: Muhammad, If I make a decision, it is not withdrawn ; and I shall not destroy them by prevailing famine, and I shall not give their control to an enemy, except from among themselves, who exterminates them en masse, even if they are stormed from all sides of the earth ; only a section of them will destroy another section, and a section will captive another section. I am afraid about my community of those leaders who will lead astray. When the sword is used among my people, it will not be withdrawn from them till the Day of Resurrection, and the Last Hour will not come before the tribes of my people attach themselves to the polytheists and tribes of my people worship idols. There will be among my people thirty great liars each of them asserting that he is (Allah's) prophet, where as I am the seal of the Prophet s after whom (me) there will be no prophet ; and a section of my people will continue to hold to the truth - (according to the Ibn Isa's version: (will continue to dominate) - the agreed version goes: ""and will not be injured by those who oppose them, till Allah's command comes."" (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4252)"
"7239","The crowd of this Ummah at the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar will be like the crowd of camels that come to drink water."
"7240","“Peace be upon you, abode of believing people. We will join you soon, if Allah wills.” Then he said: “Would that we could see our brothers.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers?” He said: “You are my Companions. My brothers are those who will come after me. I will reach the Cistern ahead of you.” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation who have not yet come?” He said: “If a man has a horse with a blaze on its forehead and white feet, don’t you think that he will recognize it among horses that are deep black in color?” They said: “Of course.” He said: “On the Day of Resurrection they will come with radiant faces, hands, and feet, because of the traces of ablution.” He said: “I will reach the Cistern ahead of you.” Then he said: “Men will be driven away from my Cistern just as stray camels are driven away. And I will call to them: ‘Come here!’ But it will be said: ‘They changed after you were gone, and they kept turning on their heels.’ So I will say: “Be off with you!” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4306)"
"7241","“My Cistern is wider than the distance between Ailah and ‘Aden. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, its vessels are more numerous than the number of stars, and it is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I will drive men away from it as a man drives strange camels away from his cistern.” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, will you recognize us?” He said: “Yes, you will come to me with radiant faces, hands and feet, because of the traces of ablution, and this is not for anyone but you.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4302)"
"7242","The people asked: O Messenger of Allah! How will you recognize those people who belong to your Ummah and whom you have not seen? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They will have radiant foreheads due to the traces of ablution."
"7243","“You will come to me with radiant faces, hands and feet from the traces of ablution. This is the characteristic sign of my nation which does not belong to anyone else.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4282)"
"7244","The narrator states: Then Sayyiduna ‘Ukasha bin Mihsan (may Allah be pleased with him) requested: O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He includes me among them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed: O Allah! Include him among them. Another person requested: Pray to Allah that He includes me among them. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Ukasha has preceded you in this regard. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""‘Ukasha has preceded you in this regard"" is, in wording, information about an action related to a past time. But by this, what is meant is to prohibit that thing for which these words are generally used, and that is: when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had already prayed for Sayyiduna ‘Ukasha (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: O Allah, include him among them, then it was not appropriate for another person to stand up (with the same request), because if the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had prayed for him as well, then a third and a fourth person would also have stood up, and the matter would have gone to such a situation for which there would be no end, and the warning of Allah Almighty which is for those people who belong to the Ummah of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and who commit prohibited acts, would become invalid (that warning is) that Allah Almighty will enter such people into Hell. Therefore, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), through verbal information, refrained from such things, and by this, what is meant is to prohibit it."
"7245","I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. The example of the Muslims among the disbelievers is like a white cow in which there is a single black hair, or a black cow in which there is a single white hair."
"7246","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, Allah Almighty has promised me that He will admit seventy thousand individuals from my Ummah into Paradise without any reckoning. Upon this, Sayyiduna Yazid bin Akhnas Salmi (may Allah be pleased with him) said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah! In your Ummah, (these seventy thousand people) will be like a handful of sand compared to a mound. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Indeed, my Lord has promised me that they will be seventy thousand people, and with each thousand, there will be seventy thousand more, and along with them, there will be some additional handfuls (i.e., the Lord will free countless people from Hell)."
"7247","I hope that He will bring my Ummah closest in the last handfuls."
"7248","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""I was shown the first of (every) three to enter Paradise: A martyr, an 'Atif, who is a Muta'affif, and a slave who perfected his worship of Allah, and was sincere to his masters."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1642)"
"7249","We offered the sunset prayer along with Allah's Apostle ﷺ. We then said: If we sit (along with Messenger of Allah) and observe night prayer with him it would be very good, so we sat down and he came to us and said: You are still sitting here. I said: Messenger of Allah, we observed evening prayer with you, then we said: Let us sit down and observe night prayer along with you, whereupon he said: You have done well or you have done right. He then lifted his head towards the sky and it often happened that as he lifted his head towards the sky, he said: The stars are a source of security for the sky and when the stars disappear there comes to the sky, i. e. (it meets the same fate) as it has been promised (it would plunge into darkness). And I am a source of safety and security to my Companions and when I would go away there would fall to the lot (of my Companions) as they have been promised with and my Companions are a source of security for the Umma and as they would go there would fall to the lot of my Umma as (its people) have been promised. (Using translation from Muslim 2531)"
"7250","The matter you have mentioned) is only related to wealth. If he has given that wealth to that person, then you should be pleased with it. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Only Ishaq has narrated this narration from Waleed, and Thawr bin Yazid has narrated only this narration from Zuhri. Only Abdullah bin Muhammad has narrated this narration from Ishaq, and this narration is extremely rare."
"7251","narrates: In the blessed era of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to consider Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), and then Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) as superior to all other companions, and then we would remain silent."
"7252","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr, and the most severe of them concerning the order of Allah is 'Umar, and the most truly modest of them is 'Uthman bin 'Affan. The best reciter (of the Qur'an) among them is Ubayy bin Ka'b, the most knowledgeable of them concerning (the laws of) inheritance is Zaid bin Thabit, the most knowledgeable of them concerning the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh bin Jabal. Truly, every nation has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this nation is Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3791)"
"7253","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Do not revile my Companions, for by The One in Whose Hand is my soul! If any one of you were to spend the equivalent of Mount Uhud in gold, it would not equal a Mudd spent by anyone of them, nor even half a Mudd."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 161)"
"7254","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood before us as I am standing before you, and said: ʿI urge you to show respect to my Companions, then those who come after them, then those who come after them, then lying will become so widespread that a man will start to give testimony before he is asked to do so.Whoever among you wants to attain a spacious abode in Paradise, let him adhere to the jama'ah (main body of Muslims), for the Shaitan is with the one who is alone, but he is further away from two. And no one of you should be alone with a woman for the Shaitan will be the third one present. The one who is pleased with his good deeds and upset by his bad deeds is a believer.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 114)"
"7255","Do not revile my Companions; by him in whose hand my soul is, if one of you contributed the amount of gold equivalent to Uhud, it would not amount to as much as the mudd of one of them, or half of it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4658)"
"7256","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""(Fear) Allah! (Fear) Allah regarding my Companions! Do not make them objects of insults after me. Whoever loves them, it is out of love of me that he loves them. And whoever hates them, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them. And whoever harms them, he has harmed me, and whoever harms me, he has offended Allah, and whoever offends Allah, [then] he shall soon be punished."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3862)"
"7257","The Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) foot was in the stirrup at that time. My collision was with your foot. I woke up at that moment. When you said: Be careful. I raised my head. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Pray for my forgiveness. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Keep moving. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to ask me about the condition in which I had left Banu Ghifar behind me. I informed you about them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: What is the condition of that group who were red in color and had no hair on their faces except for a little on the chin? I informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them staying behind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is the condition of that group whose color was black and whose hair was disheveled? I mentioned their presence among Banu Ghifar. I did not mention them until I mentioned a group that belonged to the Aslam tribe. I said: O Messenger of Allah! There is a group from the Aslam tribe, those people have stayed behind. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why have those people stayed behind? When any person among them stayed behind, then someone else should have given him his camel so that he could continue his journey in the way of Allah. To me, it is most disliked that the Muhajirun, the Ansar, or the people of the Aslam tribe, or the people of the Ghifar tribe, should stay behind me."
"7258","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ liked the Muhajirun and Ansar to stand closest to him, so that they could learn from him.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 977)"
"7259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was replying to them: ""O Allah! Indeed, true life is only the life of the Hereafter, so forgive the Ansar and the Muhajirin."
"7260","The Muhajirun and the Ansar are friends of each other in this world and the Hereafter. The Tulaqa from the Quraysh and the Utaqa from the Thaqif are friends of each other in this world and the Hereafter."
"7261","On the authority of his father (Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas): When he (Sa'd) fell ill at Mecca (according to the version of Ibn Abi Kkalaf) - then the agreed version has: which brought him near to death - the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to visit him. He said: Messenger of Allah, I have a large amount of property, and my daughter is my only heir. May I give two-thirds (of my property) as a sadaqah (charity)? He said: No. He asked: Then a half ? He replied: No. He asked: Then one-third ? He replied: (You may will away) a third and third is a lot. To leave your heirs rich is better than to leave them poor begging from people. You will not spend anything, seeking thereby to please Allah, without being rewarded for it, even the mouthful you give your wife. I said: Messenger of Allah, shall I be left behind form immigration (to Medina)? He said: If you remain behind after me and do good works seeking the pleasure of Allah, your rank will be raised and degree increased. Perhaps you will not remain behind, and some people will benefit from you and others will be harmed by you. He then said: O Allah, complete the immigration of my Companions and do not turn them back. But miserable was Sa'd b. Khawlah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ lamented on him as he died at Mecca. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2864)"
"7262","I were to give this to anyone, I would give it to my own people."
"7263","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent all of them towards Bi’r Ma’unah, and there they were all martyred. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) supplicated against their killers for several days."
"7264","A man came to Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! I am suffering from fatigue and hunger."" The Prophet ﷺ sent (somebody) to his wives (to get something), but the messenger found nothing with them. Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ said (to his companions). ""Isn't there anybody who can entertain this man tonight so that Allah may be merciful to him?"" An Ansari man got up and said, ""I (will, entertain him), O Messenger of Allah ﷺ!"" So he went to his wife and said to her, ""This is the guest of Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so do not keep anything away from him."" She said. ""By Allah, I have nothing but the children's food."" He said, ""When the children ask for their dinner, put them to bed and put out the light; we shall not take our meals tonight,"" She did so. In the morning the Ansari man went to Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said, ""Allah was pleased with (or He bestowed His Mercy) on so-and-so and his wife (because of their good deed)."" Then Allah revealed: 'But give them preference over themselves even though they were in need of that.' (59.9) (Using translation from Bukhārī 4889)"
"7265","The Ansar are my family and my trusted friends. and the people would increase in number whereas they (the Ansar) would become less and less, so appreciate the deeds of those from amongst them who do good and overlook their failings. (Using translation from Muslim 2510)"
"7266","I love you people. He said this two or three times. Then he said: Indeed, the Ansar have fulfilled that which was obligatory upon them, and now that which is obligatory upon you remains, so do good to the good among them and overlook the faults of the bad among them."
"7267","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: No harm comes to a woman who stays between the two households of the Ansar or stays with her parents."
"7268","I would choose the valley of the Ansar. The Ansar are my closest people; if there had been no migration, I would have been one of the Ansar.”"
"7269","I would have been one of the Ansar. If people were in one mountain pass and the Ansar were in another mountain pass, I would be with the Ansar in their mountain pass."
"7270","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saw some women and children of the Ansar returning from a wedding, so he said to them: ""You are the most beloved to me."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In all these narrations, the word ""minha"" will be considered omitted."
"7271","I love you people. Indeed, the Ansar have fulfilled that which was obligatory upon them. Now that which is obligatory upon you remains, so do good to their good ones and overlook the faults of their bad ones."
"7272","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah and His Messenger will love him, and whoever harbors enmity towards the Ansar, Allah and His Messenger will harbor enmity towards him. Only a believer will love them, and only a hypocrite will harbor enmity towards them.”"
"7273","Sayyiduna Harith bin Ziyad (may Allah be pleased with him), narrates that the Proph"
"7274","A person who believes in Allah and the Last Day never nurses a grudge against the Ansar. (Using translation from Muslim 76)"
"7275","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to grant the Ansar estates in Bahrain. They said: No, not unless you grant our companions from among the Quraysh something similar (we will not accept it). So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Soon after me, you will see others being given preference over you, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd (Pond of Kawthar)."
"7276","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) granted estates in Bahrain to the Ansar (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words:) granted estates to some individuals from the Ansar. They said: No, not until you grant our Muhajir brothers the same as you have granted us. We will not accept it until then. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: After me, you will face preferential treatment (given to others over you), so be patient until you meet me."
"7277","I know this about you: you refrain from asking and you are patient. Soon, after me, you will see preferential treatment in government and other matters of life, so be patient until you meet me at the Pond of Kawthar."
"7278","May Allah grant pardon to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he bestowed (these camels) upon the people of Quraish, and he ignored us, whereas our swords are still dripping blood. Anas b. Malik said: Their statement was conveyed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he sent (someone) to the Ansar and gathered them under a tent of leather. When they had assembled, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and said: What is this news that has reached me from you? The wise people of the Ansar said: Messenger of Allah, so far as the sagacious amongst us are concerned they have said nothing, but we have amongst us persons of immature age; they said: May Allah grant pardon to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he gave to the Quraish and ignored us (despite the fact) that our swords are besmeared with their blood. Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I give (at times material gifts) to persons who were quite recently in the state of unbelief, so that I may incline them to truth Don't you feel delighted that people should go with riches, and you should go back to your places with the Messenger of Allah? By Allah, that with which you would return is better than that with which they would return. They said: Yes, Messenger of Allah, we are pleased. The Prophet said too: You would find marked preference (in conferring of the material gifts) in future, so you should show patience till you meet Allah and His Messenger and I would he at the Haud Kauthar. They said: We would show patience. (Using translation from Muslim 1059a)"
"7279","Sayyiduna Usaid bin Hudair called me. I treated sciatica, and then he narrated two hadiths to"
"7280","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O Allah forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar, and the women of the Ansar."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3909)"
"7281","Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote a letter to Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) in which h"
"7282","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the grandchildren of the Ansar, and the slaves of the Ansar."
"7283","The Prophet said: “O Allah! Forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, the children of the children of the Ansar, their slaves, and their neighbors.”"
"7284","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you of the best tribe of the Ansar? Banun-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbdul Ashhal, then Banul-Harith bin al-Khazraj. then Banu Saʿidah.ʿ and he said: ʿIn each tribe of the Ansar there is goodness.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 392)"
"7285","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Shall I not tell you of the best tribe of the Ansar? Banun-Najjar, then Banu ʿAbdul Ashhal, then Banul-Harith bin al-Khazraj. then Banu Saʿidah.ʿ and he said: ʿIn each tribe of the Ansar there is goodness.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 392)"
"7286","The people said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The household of Banu Abd al-Ashhal."" These people were the family of Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Mu'adh (may Allah be pleased with him). The people asked: ""Then who, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then Banu Najjar."" The people asked: ""Then who, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then Banu Harith bin Khazraj."" The people inquired: ""Then who, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then Banu Sa'idah."" The people inquired: ""Then who, O Messenger of Allah?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is goodness in all the households of the Ansar."" When Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) was informed of this, he said: ""The Messenger of Allah mentioned us last among the four households; I will certainly speak to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about this."" Then a man said to him: ""Are you not pleased that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned you even at the end among the four households? By Allah, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) left out more households of the Ansar than he mentioned."" At this, Sayyiduna Sa'd bin Ubadah (may Allah be pleased with him) refrained."
"7291","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever belongs to the tribes of Ghifar, Aslam, Muzaynah, and Juhaynah—these people are better than the two rival tribes of Ghatafan and Banu Asad, while Hawazin and Tamim are of a lesser rank than them because they keep horses and live in deserted places."
"7292","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to them: ""O Banu Tamim, accept the glad tidings."" They replied: ""You have already given us glad tidings, now give us (wealth and property)."" Upon this, the blessed face of the Prophet (peace be upon him) changed. Then a delegation from Yemen arrived, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O people of Yemen, accept the glad tidings, because Banu Tamim did not accept this glad tidings."
"7293","The Prophet (peace be upon him) inquired: Who are you? We replied: We belong to Banu Amir. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Welcome to you people! You are from me."
"7294","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among the people of the East, the best are the people of the tribe of Abdul Qais. Other people accepted Islam by compulsion, but these people accepted Islam willingly."
"7295","""I said to Ibn 'Abbas that my grandmother makes Nabidh in an earthenware jar and it is sweet. If I drink a lot of it and sit with people, I am worried that they will find out. He said: 'The delegation of 'Abdul-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah [SAW] and he said: Welcome to a delegation that is not disgraced or filled with regret. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the idolators are between us and you, and we can only reach you during the sacred months. Tell us of something which, if we do it, we will enter Paradise, and we can tell it to those whom we left behind. He said: I will enjoin three things upon you, and forbid four things to you. I order you to have faith in Allah, and do you know what faith in Allah is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: (It means) testifying that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, establishing Salah, paying Zakah and giving one-fifth (the Khums) of the spoils of war. And I forbid four things to you: That which is soaked in Ad-Dubba', An-Naqir, Al-Hantam, and Al-Muzaffat.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 5692)"
"7296","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: \""Harshness of the heart and breaking of promises are found in the East, whereas faith is found in the land of Hijaz.\"""""
"7297","The people of Yemen have come to you; they are possessors of gentle hearts. Faith is Yemeni. Understanding is Yemeni. Wisdom (prudence) is Yemeni, whereas pride and arrogance are found among those who rear camels, while dignity is found among those who rear goats."
"7298","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Once the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was present in Madinah Munawwarah, and during that time he said: Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, Allah’s help has come, victory has come. The people of Yemen have arrived; they are people whose hearts are pure and clean, their obedience is gentle. Faith is Yemeni, understanding is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."""
"7299","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Faith is Yemeni, wisdom is Yemeni, and the root of disbelief is towards the east.\"""""
"7300","There have come the people of Yemen; they are tender of hearts, the belief is that of the Yemenites, the understanding (of the faith) is that of the Yemenites and sagacity is that of the Yemenites. (Using translation from Muslim 52a)"
"7301","that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""O Allah bless us in our Sham! O Allah bless us in our Yemen."" They said: ""And in our Najd"" He said: ""O Allah bless us in our Sham and bless us in our Yemen."" They said: ""And in our Najd"" He said: ""Earthquakes are there, and tribulations are there."" Or he said: ""The horn of Shaitan comes from there."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3953)"
"7302","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""When the people of Syria become corrupt, there will be no good left among you."
"7303","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""When the people of Syria become corrupt, there will be no good left among you."
"7304","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: We were present with you at that time, ""Glad tidings are for Syria."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The angels of the Most Merciful have spread their wings over it."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Ibn Shamasah is Abdur Rahman bin Shamasah Mahri, and he is among the trustworthy narrators of Egypt."
"7305","The narrator says: We asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! What do you command us to do then?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Stay in Sham (Greater Syria)."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The beginning of Sham is Balis and its end is Arish of Egypt."
"7306","I submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! Please choose one for me."" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is obligatory upon you to choose Sham. Whoever does not accept this should stay with his sheep and goats (away from the settlements of people), because Allah Almighty has guaranteed me (the safety of) Sham and its people."
"7307","The horses have been let loose to graze, the weapons have been put down, the war has ended, and people are saying that there will be no more fighting."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""They are wrong. Now is the time for fighting, now is the time for fighting. Indeed, Allah will turn the hearts of some people crooked, and they will begin to fight those people. Allah will continue to provide sustenance to those people until Allah's command comes to pass, and at that time, the abode of the believers will be in Syria."
"7308","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not reply. The man repeated his question. Meanwhile, Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on his shoulder and said: If faith were suspended at Thurayya (the Pleiades star), some people from his nation would attain it from there."
"7309","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""If knowledge were at Thurayya (the Pleiades star), some people from Persia would reach it.\"" (Or they would obtain it from there as well.)"""
"7310","I do not know what he instructed him: those people abused that person and beat him. That person returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and complained before him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If my messenger had gone to the people of Oman, they would not have abused him nor beaten him."
"7311","“A Jewish man said in the marketplace of Al-Madinah: ‘By the One Who chose Musa above all of mankind.’ An Ansari man raised his hand and slapped him. He said: ‘How dare you say this when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is among us?’ Mention of that was made to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: ‘Allah says: “And the trumpet will be blown, and all who are in the heavens and all who are on the earth will swoon away, except him whom Allah wills. Then it will be blown a second time, and behold they will be standing, looking on (waiting).” [39:68] I will be the first one to raise his head, and I will see Musa holding on to one of the pillars of the Throne, and I do not know whether he will have raised his head before me, or he will be one of those whom Allah exempts. And whoever says that I am better than Yunus bin Matta, he is lying.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4274)"
"7312","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: It is a horn in which it will be blown. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration is famous from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Salam (may Allah be pleased with him), but Abu Ya’la has mentioned the name of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"7313","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""Every servant will be resurrected in the state in which he died; the believer upon his faith and the hypocrite upon his hypocrisy."
"7314","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Aisha, when Allah sends punishment upon the punished people and there are righteous people among them, the punishment also befalls them. But then, according to their intentions and their deeds, they will be resurrected (on the Day of Judgment)."
"7315","I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: When Allah intends to chastise a people, He chastises all of them then they would be raised according to their deeds. (Using translation from Muslim 2879)"
"7316","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""The deceased will be resurrected in the same clothes in which he passed away.\""(Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): The deceased will be resurrected in the same clothes in which he passed away—by this, he meant the deeds of the deceased. As Allah Almighty has said: \""And purify your"
"7317",": "" "" . Ibrahim says: (The command of Allah, the Exalted, is) ""And purify your garments."" He says: This means to correct your deeds."
"7318","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""People will be resurrected (on the Day of Judgment) barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."
"7319","I heard Allah's Apostle ﷺ as saying. Every servant would be raised (in the same very state) in which he dies. (Using translation from Muslim 2878a)"
"7320","The people will be assembled on the Day of Resurrection on a white plain with a reddish tinge like the loaf of white bread with no marks set up for anyone. (Using translation from Muslim 2790)"
"7321","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""People will be resurrected (on the Day of Judgment) barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised."
"7322","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) saying during a sermon, \""You will be presented before Allah barefoot, naked, walking, and uncircumcised.\"""""
"7323","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The One Who made him walk on two feet is also able to make him walk on his face."
"7324","Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, would take in His hand His Heavens and His Earth, and would say: I am Allah. And He would clench His fingers and then would open them (and say): I am your Lord. I saw the pulpit in commotion from underneath because of something (vib-ating) there. And (I felt this commotion so much) that I said (to myself): It may not fall with Allah's Massenger ﷺ upon it. (Using translation from Muslim 2788b)"
"7325","The narrator states:) So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled until his molar teeth became visible. Then he recited this verse: ""They did not appraise Allah with true appraisal. On the Day of Resurrection, the whole earth will be in His grip, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right hand. Exalted is He and high above what they associate with Him."
"7326","The narrator says) I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) smiling, so much so that his side teeth became visible. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) smiled at the Jew’s statement, confirming his words, and then recited this verse: ""They have not appraised Allah with true appraisal; all the earth will be in His grip on the Day of Resurrection."
"7327","I am the Mighty, I am the Supreme, I am the King, I am the Dominant, I am the Honored."" Until the pulpit began to shake beneath the Prophet (peace be upon him), so we thought that it might fall."
"7328","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""People will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised (on the Day of Judgment). On the Day of Judgment, the first among the creation to be clothed will be Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him)."
"7329","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicated this by moving his blessed hand towards his mouth. The narrator says: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) indicating in this manner. Some of these people will be completely covered by their sweat. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also indicated this with his hand."
"7330","""I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: 'On the Day of Judgement, the sun will be drawn near the servants, until it has come a mile or two (away).'"" Sulaim bin 'Amir said: "" I do not know if it is miles that refer to distance on the land, or Al-Mil which is used to apply Kuhl for the eyes."" He (the Prophet ﷺ): ""The sun will melt them, until they will be in sweat according to their deeds. Among them one will be covered up to his ankles, and among them will be one who is covered up to his knees, and among them will be one who is covered up to his waist, and among them will be one who is bridled with it.' I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ indicating with his hand toward his mouth, meaning that one would be bridled with it.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2421)"
"7331","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: (Allah, the Exalted, says:) ""On that Day, people will stand before the Lord of all the worlds."" (The Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, said:) It will be a day whose length will be like fifty thousand years, until a person will be submerged in his sweat up to half of his ears."
"7332","“The Day when (all) mankind will stand before the Lord of all that exists.” [83:6] One of them will stand in his sweat up to halfway up his ears.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4278)"
"7333","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""And the people will stand before the Lord of all the worlds for a duration equal to half of that day, which is a day of fifty thousand years. This will be so easy for the Muslims as the time between the sun's nearing its rising until its setting."
"7334","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it will be easy (i.e., short) for the believer, to the extent that it will be even easier (i.e., shorter) for him than the time he used to take to perform an obligatory prayer in the world."
"7335","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""On the Day of Resurrection, a bridle of sweat will be put on the disbeliever. He will say: 'Relieve me, even if you take me to Hell.'"
"7336","Abu Huraira reported Allah's Apostle ﷺ as saying, The people will be assembled in three categories. Those desirous (of Paradise), fearing (Hell), coming two upon the came], three upon the camel, four upon the camel, ten upon the camel and the rest will be assembled, Hell-Fire being with them when they are at midday where they would spend the night and where they would spend the morning and where they would spend the evening. (Using translation from Muslim 2861)"
"7337","""The Messenger of Allah said: ""There are three to whom Allah, it Mighty and Sublime, with not speak on the Day of Resurrection: An old man who commits adultery, a poor man who is arrogant, and an Imam who tells lies.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2575)"
"7338","""Seven shall be shaded by Allah under his shade on a day in which there is no shade except His Shade: A just Imam, a young person raised upon worshiping Allah, a man whose heart is attached to the Masjid when he leaves from it until he returns from it, two men who love each other for Allah's sake, coming together upon that, and parting upon that, a man who remembers Allah in privacy and his eyes swell with tears, a man invited by a woman of status and beauty, but he says: 'I fear Allah, Mighty and Sublime is He,' and a man who conceals the charity he gives such that his left hand does not know what his right hand has spent."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2391)"
"7339","(Allah (SWT) says:) “I am the opponent of three on the Day of Resurrection, and if I am someone's opponent I will defeat him: A man who makes promises in My Name, then proves treacherous; a man who sells a free man and consumes his price; and a man who hires a worker, makes use to him, then does not give him his wages.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2442)"
"7340","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are three people to whom Allah Almighty will not look with mercy on the Day of Resurrection: one who is disobedient to his parents, one who habitually drinks alcohol, and one who reminds others of his favors after giving something."
"7341","“A banner will be set up for every traitor on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: ‘This is the treachery of so-and- so.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2872)"
"7342","Allah will set up a flag for every person guilty of breach of faith on the Day of Judgment, and it will be announced: Look, this is the perfidy of so and so. (Using translation from Muslim 1735c)"
"7343","Ibn ‘Umar reported the Apostle of Allaah ﷺ as saying “A banner will be hoisted for a treacherous man on the Day of Judgment, it will then be announced. This is a treachery of so and so, son of so and so. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2756)"
"7344","“The first matter concerning which judgment will be passed among the people on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2615)"
